# Which environment variable comes from which Vault secret (ADR-0030, TASK-0131).
#
# NAMES AND PATHS ONLY -- never a value. Format, one per line:
#   VAR=<kv-v2-mount>/<path>#<field>
# Read by skills/vault-secrets/scripts/vault_secrets.py (`exec`, `check`, `put`).
# A variable already exported in the environment wins over Vault. Every
# variable here must also appear in .env.example (tests/test-vault-secrets.sh).
#
# No entries, on purpose (TASK-0169). This repo's secrets live on a mount whose
# name is private, and this file is published through the public mirror. Each
# workstation maps them in ~/.config/vault/ai-toolbox.map, listed after this
# file in VAULT_SECRETS_MAPS:
#   GITLAB_PUSH_TOKEN   push origin (a project access token, never the admin token)
#   GITHUB_PUSH_TOKEN   push the github mirror
# The names and their meanings are in .env.example.
